  "body": "## What changed\n\nMach4 G84 now writes feeds with three metric decimals or four inch decimals.\nThe post refuses a tap if the written F/S pitch differs by more than 0.01 percent.\nThe diagnostic names G84 and the operation.\nOther feed moves keep their existing formatter.\n\n## Cause\n\nG84 used the general feed formatter, which kept one metric decimal or two inch decimals.\nFor example, 34.56 mm/min became F34.6 without a warning.\nInch conversion and integer spindle speeds can also change the written pitch.\n\n## Tests\n\nEffort: high.\nThe tested final tree is commit `9e311f317c9d45376f94a578327da05d834908ce`.\nThe branch starts at upstream `d54580cad`.\nValidation used the current upstream reference `37aca7f8c`.\nThe gate used merge base `d54580cad` for this branch's three changed files.\n\nPins in `mach4_feed_decimals`:\n\n- `mach4_g84_keeps_two_and_three_mm_feed_decimals`\n- `mach4_g84_keeps_four_inch_feed_decimals`\n- `mach4_refuses_tap_feed_rounding_that_changes_pitch`\n- `mach4_refuses_tap_speed_rounding_that_changes_pitch`\n\nAll four pins failed on the unchanged Mach4 script before the fix.\nThe old script wrote F34.6 instead of F34.56 and F1.36 instead of F1.3606.\nIt emitted G84 without the expected pitch diagnostic in both refusal cases.\nAll four pins pass with the fix.\n\nMutation results:\n\n- Restore the old formatter: both precision pins fail. The refusal pins pass.\n- Remove the pitch guard: both refusal pins fail. The precision pins pass.\n- Copy the complete script from `git show upstream/main:assets/posts/mach4.cps`: all four pins fail.\n- Restore the fix: all four pins pass.\n\nFinal checks:\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test mach4_feed_decimals`: 4 passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 63 steps passed, 0 failed, 0 stalled.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed.\n- The quick gate ran `script_mach4` and the three `example_catalog*` suites. All passed.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run`: no post heavy step exists.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --only post`: 0 steps ran; exit 2, no matching step.\n\nThe new test binary pins numeric tap feeds and pitch refusals.\nNo Mach4 domain directory suite exists.\nThe decision file records the chosen formatter, guard, and alternatives.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\nThe Mach4 recorded golden suite and `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, and `example_catalog_edge_work` passed.\n`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` produced no output.\nNo recorded programs changed, so no regeneration was needed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo physical Mach4 control or cutting test ran.\nNo full heavy lane ran because no post heavy step or ignored tap test exists.\nThe heavy plan reached only the unrelated `app heavy: probe_no_coolant` suite, which was excluded.\nThere is no UI change, so no screenshots are needed.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone.\nChecks covered all three changed files and all open PRs before the push.\n\nChangelog: Mach4 keeps G84 tap feed precision and refuses written pitch errors above 0.01 percent.\n\nFixes #3701\n",
